  "tag_ids": [],
  "policy_sha256": "84f656b16099dcb248866f714453e5bd3e275bdb5d4929c4fad838ee8b29ed2c",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00001",
      "text": "Abubakar Idris Dadiyata, a lecturer and fierce critic of the Nigerian government, was abducted from his home on August 1, 2019, in the Barnawa neighbourhood of Kaduna, in northwestern Nigeria.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "body_start": 0,
      "body_end": 192,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00002",
      "text": "One year after his abduction, Dadiyata has not been found.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 2,
      "body_start": 194,
      "body_end": 252,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00003",
      "text": "Dadiyata taught at Federal University Dutsinma, Katsina State. As a member of the opposition Peoples Democratic Party, Dadiyata often sparred with members of the ruling All Progressive Congress party on social media.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 3,
      "body_start": 254,
      "body_end": 470,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00004",
      "text": "Read more: Apprehension rises over the abduction of a Nigerian government critic",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 4,
      "body_start": 472,
      "body_end": 552,
      "source_links": [
        "https://globalvoices.org/2019/08/16/apprehension-rises-over-the-abduction-of-a-nigerian-government-critic/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "h4",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00005",
      "text": "‘Both the state and federal agencies are busy doing nothing’",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 5,
      "body_start": 554,
      "body_end": 614,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "h3",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00006",
      "text": "Dadiyata was forcefully taken by abductors at about 1 a.m. as he arrived at his home, a year ago on August 1, 2019, Premium Times reported.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 6,
      "body_start": 616,
      "body_end": 755,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.premiumtimesng.com/regional/nwest/344451-top-ganduje-critic-kidnapped-in-kaduna.html"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00007",
      "text": "Kadija, Dadiyata’s wife recalls in an interview with BBC that her husband was “making a phone call, his car was still running,” when he was seized by his abductors. Although Kadija could not hear what “ensued over the phone or who he was talking to,” she recalled that her husband's abductors “had followed him, they even came into the house.” Dadiyata’s wife watched from her room as they drove her husband away.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 7,
      "body_start": 757,
      "body_end": 1170,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/p08q45kz"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00008",
      "text": "Sadly, there’s still no information about Dadiyata’s whereabouts. “It is painful,” Kadija told the BBC, as their children keep asking about their missing father.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 8,
      "body_start": 1172,
      "body_end": 1333,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/p08q45kz"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00009",
      "text": "Rather than finding Dadiyata, Nigerian security agencies are absolving themselves from any form of guilt or blame for his disappearance.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 9,
      "body_start": 1335,
      "body_end": 1471,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00010",
      "text": "Nigeria’s Department of State Security (DSS) had in January denied having Dadiyata in their custody. The state security agency stated that since Dadiyata “was taken away from his house by some armed men does not suggest that those men were DSS staff.”",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 10,
      "body_start": 1473,
      "body_end": 1724,
      "source_links": [
        "https://observerstimes.com/hes-not-in-our-custody-dss-breaks-silence-on-dadiyata/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00011",
      "text": "Similarly, Aisha Dikko, the attorney general of Kaduna State, denied knowing the “whereabouts” or of being involved “whatsoever” in Dadiyata’s abduction. “Anything to the contrary is a vile assertion that seeks to stretch the fact that he was abducted within Kaduna State to mean the involvement of the state government,” said Dikko.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 11,
      "body_start": 1726,
      "body_end": 2059,
      "source_links": [
        "https://dailynigerian.com/kaduna-govt-denies-involvement-in-dadiyatas-abduction/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00012",
      "text": "However, these denials by DSS and Kaduna State Government neither mitigates the agony of Dadiyata’s wife and their two children — nor does it restore his liberty.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 12,
      "body_start": 2061,
      "body_end": 2223,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00013",
      "text": "The plea for Dadiyata’s release still echoes on Twitter in this hashtag #OneYearWithOutDadiyata, as Nigerians demand his release.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 13,
      "body_start": 2225,
      "body_end": 2354,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00014",
      "text": "Bulama Bukarti lamented about the “trauma” that this “kind of impunity” has caused Dadiyata's family:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 14,
      "body_start": 2356,
      "body_end": 2457,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00015",
      "text": "This Twitter user was “shattered” on hearing Dadiyata's wife interview:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 15,
      "body_start": 2459,
      "body_end": 2530,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00016",
      "text": "Akin Akíntáyọ̀ cannot understand how Dadiyata can “disappear without a trace for a year:”",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 16,
      "body_start": 2532,
      "body_end": 2621,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00017",
      "text": "Unfortunately, it seems as if nobody cares about finding the critic.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 17,
      "body_start": 2623,
      "body_end": 2691,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00018",
      "text": "Rather “both the state and federal agencies are busy” avoiding blame and “doing nothing” states human rights activist Professor Chidi Odinkalu in an interview with Vyral Africa:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 18,
      "body_start": 2693,
      "body_end": 2870,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x-UxObHiIL8&feature=youtu.be"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-717280-b00019",
      "text": "> Besides saying that they don’t know where he is. Nobody has really made the effort to tell us what they have done to find him and how it is that they can’t account for him. It tells you how so little we matter as citizens. The least we can do is ask where Dadiyata is and why can’t our government find him.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 19,
      "body_start": 2872,
      "body_end": 3180,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    }
  ],
